    "steps": [
      "Slice the pork loin about 1/4 inch (6 mm) thick. Pound the slices gently with a meat mallet to make them a little thinner.",
      "Season both sides of the pork lightly with salt and pepper. Coat each slice in the flour in a shallow dish and shake off the extra.",
      "Melt the butter for frying in a large skillet on medium-high, together with the olive oil.",
      "Lay the pork in the pan in one layer, working in batches if needed. Cook 3 minutes on each side, until golden and 145°F (63°C) inside.",
      "Move the pork to a plate.",
      "Add the chicken stock, capers and lemon juice to the pan. Scrape up the browned bits and boil until reduced by about a third.",
      "Taste the sauce for salt and pepper. Swirl in the remaining butter until the sauce turns glossy and slightly thick.",
      "Arrange the pork on plates, spoon the sauce over and sprinkle with the parsley.",
      "You nailed it! Grab a plate and dig in."
